# Settings › Home server › Alerts & power (docs/HOME-SERVER.md): spins down idle data drives (hdparm, never the system
# drive), keeps the PC awake while your devices use it, and lets it sleep when nobody needs it: never while Game Mode
# runs, a share is open or a backup runs, and never past anything else holding sleep off. Started only by its timer,
# off until you turn a power choice on. Never part of starting the PC, the session or Game Mode.
[Unit]
Description=Hearth home server: power

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/libexec/nimbus/hearth-home-server-helper power run
Nice=10
TimeoutStartSec=5min
